  <issue>
  Re-enter insert/passthrough mode after temporarily leaving it
Qutebrowser shouldn't change modes unless the user wants to. As an example of when this occurs, when you're in `passthrough` mode, saving an image by *right click* > *save* will return you to `normal` mode instead of `passthrough`.

Maybe it's possible to have each command, that potentially changes the active mode, restore the previous mode before exit. Either by not storing the state anywhere and passing it as arguments (like in functional programming):

	def my_command(qb_state, ...): # qb_state: current state of qutebrowser, incl. current mode
		... # do something
		return qb_state

Or like this:

	def my_command(qb_state, ...):
		prev_mode = qb_state.mode
		... # do something
		qb_state.mode = prev_mode
		return

Either way, since only one command is executed at a time, the call stack would do all the work. 

Commands, that change tabs, would leave the state alone, allowing each tab to have its own state.
  </issue>
  
